# DWPlusFP: a double-word number plus a number of the format.
kernel:        add_2_1
input:         x = x0 x1
input:         a
output:        z = z0 z1
value:         x+a
requires:      normalized x
ensures:       normalized z
ensures:       error z R c=2 k=2 t=0
min_precision: 3
theorem:       proofs/theories/Add21.v add_2_1_correct
source:        JMP17 Alg. 4 (DWPlusFP); bound from MR22
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
guard_pending: a milestone1.md guards a in the first line (g = guard(a)), which changes the formal model of this proved kernel: the guard lands with its proof. Until then the public headers guard a before the call

(sh, sl) = two_sum(x0, a)
v        = add(x1, sl)
(z0, z1) = fast_two_sum(sh, v)
